SOURCE NOTE: found while benchmarking the #137 Single Number II kata (kara-katas leetcode/101-200/137-single-number-ii/bench). The hot loop is the kata's own per-bit count-mod-3 variant, written the only natural way:

  while i < nums.len() {
      if ((nums[i] >> b) & 1i64) == 1i64 {
          cnt = cnt + 1i64;
      }
      i = i + 1i64;
  }

MEASURED (x86-64 container, 4 arrays of 120,001 i64, 40 punches, 30 runs + 5 warmup): kara 281.3ms +/- 4.4, rust -O -C overflow-checks=on 277.2 +/- 8.9, rust -O 37.4 +/- 3.1, clang -O3 35.2 +/- 1.4, go 112.7 +/- 10.3. kara ties the equal-safety Rust build to within 1.5% (inside sigma); both are 7.9x behind the two builds allowed to wrap silently. This is the sharpest equal-safety split in the kata corpus.

