    as above                                                   LEAK 8 B / 1
    `Result[Vec[P], i64]` instead of Option                    LEAK 8 B / 1
    3 elements, 10-byte strings                                LEAK 30 B / 3  (linear: 1/elem)
    `match mk() { ... }` -- INLINE, no `let`                    clean
    `let held = mk(); let v = held.unwrap();`                   clean  (match is required)
    `let _held = mk();` -- bound but never used                 clean
    payload `Vec[String]` -- no struct layer                    clean
    payload `P` -- no Vec layer                                 clean
    struct with only a scalar field                             clean

So leg B needs BOTH container layers (Vec of a heap-bearing struct -- either alone is clean), the `let` binding, and consumption by `match` specifically (`unwrap` is clean, and never using it is clean).

